.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH murk-env 1  "env " 
.SH NAME
murk\-env \- Write a .envrc for direnv integration
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmurk env\fR [\fB\-\-vault\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Write a .envrc for direnv integration
.PP
Creates `.envrc` in the current directory with a line that runs `murk export`. If `.envrc` already exists, murk appends the line. If it already has a `murk export` line, murk changes nothing. Run `direnv allow` afterward.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-vault\fR \fI<VAULT>\fR [default: .murk]
Vault filename
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
